lerna-debug.log*

node_modules

# Package checkouts, cloned by scripts/setup.mjs. Anchored to the repository root so a directory
# that happens to share one of these names further down is not silently untracked.
/epicurrents/*
/interface
/ohif
/util
/build
/dist
/vendor
*.local

# The root lock file is committed, because scripts/manifest.mjs does not pin dependency versions:
# it records each package's commit, so two setups of one manifest can still resolve different
# versions of everything the packages depend on, and an edition built twice is not the same bytes.
#
# A lock file only binds here because setup clones every selected package before installing once.
# Its workspace entries are links into those checkouts, so they resolve only if the directories
# already exist, and an install run per package instead prunes the entries of packages not yet
# cloned and re-resolves them on arrival.
#
# What is committed therefore describes one workspace: every public package, which is what a release
# builds and what `--frozen-lockfile` checks `npm ci` against. A profile-scoped setup clones a subset
# and a maintainer's tree adds the private packages, and an install in either rewrites the file. Do
# not commit that rewrite; a release would fail in `npm ci` against a checkout it does not describe.

# Private build profiles — editions that may reference non-public packages.
# The folder and its README stay tracked; the profile files do not.
/profiles/local/*
!/profiles/local/README.md

